  bootwright / context init
      Initialize and select a context. Import desired state from one YAML file with --file or
      from a directory with --input-dir. To use both flags, pass a standalone Context with
      --file.

  Usage
    bootwright context init [flags]

  Command flags
      --check      Check admission without publishing anything
      -f, --file   Read one YAML file containing desired state or a standalone Context
      --input-dir  Import an Environment input directory
      --name       Select the exact object name (required)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright context init --name lab --file ./environment.yaml
